% ============================================================================
% part-of-speech.query.adj — a worked recall over the part-of-speech
% library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what part of speech is
% this word?": it states no fact of its own — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?`
% against the `part_of_speech` rows and returns the category + the table's
% own source/locator/trust. A word the table does not carry abstains
% honestly — the engine never invents a classification.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli part-of-speech.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "part-of-speech.adj"

? part_of_speech(queen, $Category)          % expect noun
? part_of_speech($Word, verb)               % expect run
? part_of_speech(quietly, $Category)        % expect adverb (newly added row)
? part_of_speech($Word, preposition)        % expect against (newly added row)
? part_of_speech(slowly, $Category)         % expect abstain — no category is shipped for this word
